### Product Inventory API - sample requests
### Works with the "REST Client" extension for VS Code (click "Send Request").

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@json = application/json

### Health check (verifies database connectivity)
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### Create a product (201). Repeat it to get 409 Conflict.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "name": "Laptop Pro 15",
  "sku": "LAP-100",
  "description": "15 inch laptop",
  "price": 1299.99,
  "stock_quantity": 10,
  "status": "active"
}

### Validation error (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "name": "", "sku": "bad sku", "price": -5, "status": "unknown" }

### List products with pagination (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?page=1&page_size=5

### Filter by status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?status=active

### Search by name (case-insensitive, partial)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?q=laptop

### Low stock products (stock_quantity <= 5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?low_stock=true

### Get one product (200, or 404 if it does not exist, 400 if the id is invalid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/1

### Partial update (200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/1
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "price": 1199.00, "stock_quantity": 8 }

### Update with PUT (same behaviour as PATCH: only the given fields change)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/1
Content-Type: {{json}}

{ "status": "archived" }

### Delete a product (204 No Content)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/1
